The upstream_check module adds active health checks to nginx upstreams:
nginx probes each backend on a timer and takes a failing one out of the
balancer before a request lands on it, instead of discovering the failure
with somebody's request.

Unlike the other nginx module ports this one also ships the patches for
nginx itself, one per server flavour.  The check state has to reach every
balancer, and stock nginx offers a module no way in, so round robin,
hash, ip_hash and least_conn are hooked by patch.  The nginx ports apply
the one that fits and build the module into the binary when their
HTTP_UPSTREAM_CHECK option is enabled.

This port only installs the sources and those patches.
